    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Adjunct-Faculty---SML_JR10046": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - SML",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app The Sport Management and Leadership program within the Department of Kinesiology is seeking in person adjunct faculty members to teach undergraduate courses during Spring 2027. Courses include: SML 565 Principles of Coaching SML 631 Sport Media Production SML 738 Sport Finance SML 740 Athletic Administration Adjunct faculty members will be responsible for delivering course content, facilitating student learning, assessing student performance, and providing appropriate academic support in accordance with established course objectives and program expectations. The scope of responsibility is limited primarily to instruction and student support associated with the assigned course(s). Duties/Responsibilities Course Instruction – 80% Teach assigned undergraduate course(s) in the Sport Management and Leadership program, which may include Sport Finance, Sport Media Production, Principles of Coaching and Athletic Administration. Prepare and deliver course content consistent with established course objectives and learning outcomes. Develop and manage course materials, assignments, assessments, and other learning activities.   Student Assessment and Support – 20% Evaluate student performance and provide timely feedback on assignments, examinations, and other course requirements. Communicate course expectations clearly and provide reasonable academic support to students enrolled in the course.   Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience: Master’s degree in Sport Management, Sport Administration, Business, or a closely related field. College-level teaching experience relevant to the course(s) to be taught is required.   Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Strong knowledge of the subject matter relevant to the assigned course(s). Ability to effectively teach and communicate course content to undergraduate students. Ability to develop and deliver organized, engaging, and academically appropriate course materials and learning activities. Ability to assess student learning and provide clear and timely feedback. Strong interpersonal and communication skills and the ability to work effectively with students from diverse backgrounds and experiences. Ability to use instructional technology and learning management systems to support course delivery.   Preferred Qualifications: Relevant professional or sport industry experience is preferred. Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents)   Resume/CV Cover Letter Contact Information for 3 Professional References Compensation Pay Range: 1-2 credit courses $3,100 3-4 credit courses $6,100 The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham Salary Grade: Period Activity"
